{
  "$comment": [
    "Where the Ecore models come from, and in which order they may be loaded.",
    "",
    "The models are copied into packages/xmla-model/model/ and committed, so this",
    "repository builds without a Java toolchain and without a 100 MB checkout. The",
    "copies are guarded by a sha256 manifest: `npm run check:sync` fails when they",
    "drift from the source. That turns drift into a red build instead of a silent",
    "difference nobody notices until a rowset reads wrong.",
    "",
    "`sourceRoot` may be overridden with the XMLA_MODEL_SOURCE environment variable.",
    "",
    "`models` is in topological order, computed from the eType cross-references",
    "(`eType=\"ecore:EClass <nsURI>#//Name\"`). Cross-model types resolve through the",
    "package registry by nsURI, so every dependency has to be registered first.",
    "The graph is acyclic; `dependsOn` records it so the order stays checkable"
  ],
  "sourceRoot": "/home/stbischof/git/daanse/org.eclipse.daanse.xmla",
  "models": [
